/** @mainpage %Qore sshutil Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section sshutilintro sshutil Module Introduction

    The %sshutil binary module provides typed SSH client identity provider,
    SSH server host-key provider, and remote host-key trust-store contracts for
    binary modules and Qore code.

    The module defines only generic SSH vocabulary: hosts, ports, usernames,
    public-key metadata, short-lived private-key material descriptors, host-key
    trust decisions, provider context fields, and registry names.  Storage,
    tenancy, authorization, and secret-manager integration belong to embedding
    applications and are passed through only as opaque context.

    @section sshutiloverview API Overview

    The main abstract classes are:

    - @ref Qore::SshUtil::AbstractSshClientIdentityProvider for ordered client
      public-key authentication candidates
    - @ref Qore::SshUtil::AbstractSshServerHostKeyProvider for listener host
      identity key material
    - @ref Qore::SshUtil::AbstractSshHostKeyStore for remote host-key
      verification, TOFU acceptance, and explicit approval

    The module also provides descriptor-only filesystem providers preserving
    existing file-path based behavior where callers explicitly choose it, plus
    @ref Qore::SshUtil::SshUtilRegistry for runtime lookup by stable names.

    @section sshutilreleasenotes sshutil Module Release Notes

    This module is always delivered with %Qore and therefore mirrors the %Qore
    version.
*/
